# =============================================================================
# OPEN QUESTIONS — must be resolved before this file is production-ready
# (copied from spec; answers drive the TODO replacements above)
# =============================================================================
#
# Q1. What language and runtime version does the project use?
#     → Determines: runtime setup action/image, SAST analyser, linter choice.
#
# Q2. What build tool and package manager is in use?
#     → Determines: install command, dependency cache paths, lockfile name.
#
# Q3. What test runner and reporting format is in use?
#     → Determines: test command, artifact paths, JUnit XML report path.
#
# Q4. Which CI/CD platform is the team using?
#     → Determines: which section of this file to keep and where to save it.
#
# Q5. Which SAST tool is preferred?
#     → GitHub Actions: CodeQL (Option A), Semgrep (Option B), or Trivy (Option C).
#     → GitLab CI: built-in SAST template (already included above).
#     → Shell: Semgrep, Trivy, Bandit, or other CLI tool.
#
# Q6. What is the default/protected branch name?
#     → Determines: trigger branch filters in the pipeline definition.
#
# Q7. Are there branch protection rules to enforce pipeline status checks?
#     → Determines: whether additional repository settings changes are needed
#       alongside this pipeline configuration.
#
# Q8. What SAST severity threshold should fail the build?
#     → Determines: severity filter values in the SAST tool configuration.
#
# =============================================================================